# buildment invariants

Full detail lives in [AGENTS.md](../../AGENTS.md) and `docs/` — this is the short version so it's
always in context.

- Never send `Block.config` (answers, rubrics, hidden tests, sample answers) to the client. Server-only.
- `Quiz`/`Test` grading is server-side only. `CodeBlock` check results are client-reported and must
  be labeled as such wherever shown.
- Gating (sequential chapters, blocking blocks) is enforced on the server data loader — a locked
  chapter returns 403, never just a hidden UI link.
- One interactive block type = one entry in `src/blocks/<type>/` registered in
  `src/blocks/registry.ts`. Never special-case a `BlockType` outside its own folder.
- `Response` rows are append-only. Fix progress by writing a new attempt + recomputing rollups, never by mutating a response.
- All authorization goes through `server/auth/guards.ts`. No ad-hoc per-route checks.
- Reports read only denormalized tables (`ChapterProgress`, `Enrollment`) — never aggregate over `Response` on the read path.

If a task seems to require breaking one of these, stop and flag it instead of working around it.
